### Variables
@baseUrl = http://localhost:4000
@email = test-{{$timestamp}}@example.com

### 1. Test Registration WITH Company & Branch
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Test User With Branch",
  "email": "{{email}}",
  "password": "SecurePass123!",
  "company_id": "COMP1",
  "branch_id": "BR001"
}

### 2. Test Registration WITH Company Only (No Branch)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Test User No Branch",
  "email": "test-nobranch-{{$timestamp}}@example.com",
  "password": "SecurePass123!",
  "company_id": "COMP1"
}

### 3. Test Registration WITHOUT Company & Branch (Should still work)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Test User No Company",
  "email": "test-nocompany-{{$timestamp}}@example.com",
  "password": "SecurePass123!"
}

### 4. Query Database - Check last user created
# Jalankan di SQL Server Management Studio atau tools SQL lainnya:
# SELECT TOP 5 id, name, email, company_id, branch_id, emailVerified 
# FROM sys_User 
# ORDER BY id DESC;

### 5. Get All Companies (untuk cek company_id yang valid)
GET {{baseUrl}}/sys_company

### 6. Get All Branches (untuk cek branch_id yang valid)
GET {{baseUrl}}/sys_branch

### 7. Get Branches by Company ID
GET {{baseUrl}}/sys_branch/company/COMP1

